# Database & SQL

## Thin backend

Heavy aggregations belong in SQL (views/RPCs), not application loops over raw
rows. If a view lacks a field, propose `ALTER VIEW` / a migration rather than
patching in app code.

## Row Level Security (mandatory)

Every new user-data table must `ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY` and define at least
one `CREATE POLICY`. See `verify-rls-policies`.

## Migration workflow (isolated-test first)

1. `supabase migration new`; never edit applied historical migrations.
2. Validate on the project's isolated test DB (discover bootstrap from README /
   package scripts). Never mutate personal-local as a verification step.
3. Regenerate generated DB types from the test DB URL.
4. Remote push requires a separate explicit user instruction.
5. NEVER run `supabase db reset` (or the project's wipe-local equivalent) unless
   the human explicitly asks.

## Anti-drift

After schema changes, refresh the project's database inventory doc if `doc-routing`
maps one.
